<title>USA: USDA says to allow beef imports from Argentina.</title>
<headline>USDA says to allow beef imports from Argentina.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Tuesday said it will allow fresh, chilled and frozen beef imports from Argentina as of August 25.</p>
<p>&quot;We are confident that importing meat from Argentina will not put domestic livestock at risk,&quot; said Joan Arnoldi, an official with USDA's Animal and Plant Health Inspection Service.</p>
<p>The final rule will be published in the Federal Register on June 26.</p>
<p>The move ends a 67-year-old ban on beef shipments from Argentina.</p>
